sequenceDiagram
    title UC-01: Pipeline IA Asíncrono (Celery Worker)

    participant R as Redis Queue
    participant W as Celery Worker
    participant S3 as S3/MinIO
    participant TS as TorchServe GPU
    participant PG as PostgreSQL
    participant WS as WebSocket Manager

    R->>W: Consume tarea {sample_id, s3_path, chn_code}
    W->>S3: GET imagen por chn_code (nunca por PII)
    S3-->>W: Stream imagen TIFF

    W->>W: CLAHE preprocessing (clipLimit=3.0, tileGridSize=8x8)
    W->>W: Tiling 1024x1024 + overlap 64px (si imagen >4K)

    loop Por cada tile
        W->>TS: POST /predictions/unet_karyotype {tile_base64}
        TS-->>W: {polygons, bounding_boxes, masks}
    end

    W->>W: NMS — elimina duplicados en bordes de tiles

    loop Batch de 16 cromosomas
        W->>TS: POST /predictions/efficientnet_b3 {crops_base64}
        TS-->>W: [{pair_number, confidence_score}] x16
    end

    W->>PG: INSERT 46 chromosomes (pair, score, polygon, requires_review)
    W->>PG: UPDATE samples SET status='ready'
    W->>WS: Redis PubSub PUBLISH "sample:{id}:events" {status:"ready", count:46}
    WS-->>UI: WebSocket push — "Borrador listo 🔔"

    Note over W,TS: Si TorchServe falla → modo degradado manual
